{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791237035,"nonce":"QYPHcqDUBBvvX7YsmOSnUyRAdpI=","title":"An abstract method that assigns `this` does not write back to the variable it was called on","message":"var f = new haxe.EnumFlags\u003cMyEnum\u003e();\n    f.set(B);\n    trace(f.toInt()); // 0, Haxe prints 2\n\n`EnumFlags.set` is `inline function set(v:T) this |= 1 \u003c\u003c Type.enumIndex(v);`. In Haxe, assigning `this` inside an abstract method over a value type updates the receiver when it is a local or field. Rayzor updates a copy, so `set`/`unset` on a local `EnumFlags` (and any similar abstract) has no effect.\n\nProbe: scratchpad p2224 (nuc ~/probes/p2224). Related: 09019f0 (a mutating `next()` on an abstract iterator loops forever).","files":null}]}